# MerchantShield AI — environment configuration
#
# The backend (FastAPI) currently reads NO environment variables. All paths
# (model artifact, metadata, audit database) are computed relative to the project
# root in backend/config/settings.py and are not configurable via environment at
# this time -- documented here explicitly rather than leaving that undocumented.
#
# The only environment variable used anywhere in this project is optional, and
# only affects the frontend during local development.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (frontend/.env, optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL the dashboard uses for API calls. Leave unset (or copy this file as
# frontend/.env with this line uncommented) only if you're running the Vite dev
# server (`npm run dev`) separately from the backend, e.g. on a different port.
#
# When the frontend is built (`npm run build`) and served by FastAPI itself
# (the normal production path -- see backend/main.py's StaticFiles mount), this
# is unnecessary: the built app calls the API same-origin and this variable
# should stay unset.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
